INT. COUNTY FAIR - SOURDOUGH PAVILION - DAY

A striped canvas tent crowded with trestle tables. Loaves arranged under glass cloches like jewels. A hand-lettered banner: GOLDEN CRUST CHAMPIONSHIP. The air smells of yeast and burnt sugar.

BEATRICE "BEA" HALLORAN, 60s, in a flour-dusted apron and her late husband's flat cap, guards a crusty round loaf with the tenderness of a mother with her firstborn.

OKSANA PRYSTAI, 50s, her lifelong rival, in a ruffled blouse and bright red lipstick, tends a loaf of her own. She is the picture of calm, and she sweats.

JUDGE ARMAND DELACOUR, 70s, in a straw boater and a white linen suit, strolls the tables with a tasting knife and the face of a man who has seen it all.

His assistant, LIAM, 19, in an apron three sizes too big, trots after him with a notebook and a pencil he can't keep sharp.

DELACOUR
(to Liam)
Write this down. Table four. Crust, firm. Crumb, open. Aroma, hints of sour cherry.

LIAM
Sour cherry?

DELACOUR
I find it on the nose.

Beatrice lifts her cloche with a flourish. Steam curls. Delacour leans in. Oksana, at the next table, cranes sideways. Liam drops his pencil, retrieves it, drops it again. Beatrice sets the loaf on its board, tears it with her bare hands, and holds out a steaming half. Delacour accepts it, chews, and closes his eyes. Oksana dabs her upper lip with a handkerchief. Liam writes something illegible.

DELACOUR (CONT'D)
Beatrice. This is magnificent.

BEA
Thank you, Armand.

DELACOUR
Is that rye?

BEA
A little.

DELACOUR
It sings.

OKSANA
(muttering)
It screams.

BEA
I heard that, Oksana.

OKSANA
You were meant to.

Delacour moves on to table five. Oksana lifts her own cloche with an equally grand gesture. He tastes. He chews. He frowns.

DELACOUR
Hm.

OKSANA
Hm?

DELACOUR
It is very... confident.

LIAM
(whispering)
Is that good?

DELACOUR
It is not bad.

Oksana's smile cracks. Beatrice turns away to hide a grin. Delacour clears his throat and consults Liam's notes.

DELACOUR (CONT'D)
The winner is table four.

Beatrice lets out a little shriek, grabs her flat cap, and flings it into the air. It lands on Liam's head. Oksana stares at her loaf as though it has betrayed her.

OKSANA
Next year.

BEA
Next year.

They shake hands. It lasts a beat too long.
